---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import MoreInCategory from "../components/MoreInCategory.astro";
import { authorSchema, authorName } from "../data/authors";
import AuthorAvatar from "../components/AuthorAvatar.astro";
import QuickPicks from "../components/QuickPicks.astro";
import PlanTheJob from "../components/PlanTheJob.astro";
import AuthorBio from "../components/AuthorBio.astro";
import { amazonLink } from "../data/affiliate";
import TrustBadge from "../components/TrustBadge.astro";
import SocialProof from "../components/SocialProof.astro";
import productImages from "../data/product-images.json";
import { pageDates } from "../data/dates";

const moreInCategory = [
  {
    "title": "Best Cordless Vacuums",
    "url": "/best-cordless-vacuum/"
  },
  {
    "title": "Best Robot Vacuums",
    "url": "/best-robot-vacuum/"
  },
  {
    "title": "Robot Vacuum vs Regular Vacuum",
    "url": "/robot-vacuum-vs-regular-vacuum/"
  },
  {
    "title": "Are Robot Vacuums Worth It?",
    "url": "/are-robot-vacuums-worth-it/"
  },
  {
    "title": "Best Carpet Cleaners",
    "url": "/best-carpet-cleaner/"
  },
  {
    "title": "Shop Vac vs Regular Vacuum",
    "url": "/shop-vac-vs-regular-vacuum/"
  },
  {
    "title": "Best Air Purifier for Allergies",
    "url": "/best-air-purifier-for-allergies/"
  }
];
const dates = pageDates(Astro.url.pathname, { published: "2026-10-30", modified: "2026-10-30" });
const title = "7 Best Vacuum Cleaners in 2026: Picked by What You Prefer";
const description =
  "Upright, canister, cordless or robot? Seven vacuum cleaners matched to your floors, pets, allergies and budget, with the trade-offs spelled out.";

const PRODUCTS = [
  {
    "id": "shark-navigator-lift-away",
    "name": "Shark Navigator Lift-Away Upright",
    "category": "Bagless Upright, Budget",
    "badge": "Best Overall Value",
    "amazonUrl": "#",
    "pros": [
      "Bagless canister with a Lift-Away pod that detaches for stairs, furniture and above-floor jobs",
      "Sold with a sealed-system filter design that Shark markets for allergy households",
      "Swivel steering makes it easy to turn around furniture legs",
      "Corded power means no battery to degrade and no runtime to watch",
      "Widely stocked, with replacement filters and parts easy to find"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "Heavier than a stick vacuum, and the cord limits how far you can roam",
      "Washable filters need regular cleaning or suction drops off"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "The vacuum we would point most households toward first: one machine that handles carpet, hard floor and stairs without a four-figure price.",
    "description": "The Navigator Lift-Away earns the top spot because it asks the least of the buyer. It is a conventional corded upright with a bagless dust cup, which means there is no battery to wear out and no bag to keep stocking. The feature that sets it apart from older uprights is the Lift-Away pod: the canister and wand release from the body so you can carry the motor and clean stairs, upholstery and ceiling corners without wrestling the whole machine. Shark markets the model with a sealed system and a HEPA-style filter for allergy households, and owners commonly report that it pulls pet hair off low-pile carpet well. The brush roll is a standard bristle design, so long hair can wrap it and you will need to cut it free every few weeks. It is also on the heavier side compared with a cordless stick. If you want one affordable, dependable, easy-to-repair vacuum that does everything adequately, start here and only move up if a specific preference below pushes you elsewhere."
  },
  {
    "id": "miele-complete-c3-calima",
    "name": "Miele Complete C3 Calima Canister",
    "category": "Bagged Canister, Sealed System",
    "badge": "Best for Allergies &amp; Longevity",
    "amazonUrl": "#",
    "pros": [
      "Bagged, sealed-system design keeps dust contained when you empty it",
      "Canister layout is easy on hard floors, stairs, curtains and tight spots",
      "Miele builds the Complete C3 range for long service life and sells replacement parts and bags",
      "Long reach from the hose and cord lets you clean a room without unplugging",
      "Quiet running compared with many bagless uprights, according to owner reports"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "Premium price and a recurring cost for replacement bags and filters",
      "A canister is awkward on big areas of thick carpet unless you add a powered floor head"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "The pick for allergy sufferers and anyone who wants a vacuum to last a decade, as long as you accept the bag and the higher purchase price.",
    "description": "Miele is the brand most often recommended when someone says they want a vacuum that will outlast two cheaper ones, and the Complete C3 Calima is the model that makes the case. It is a canister, so the motor stays on the floor and you move only a light wand, which is easier on the wrist and far better on stairs and bare floor than hauling an upright. It uses disposable bags inside a sealed system, so the dust you collect stays inside the bag rather than puffing out when you empty a bin. Miele specifies filtration aimed at allergy households, and the bagged design is the main reason this category is so often suggested for them. The trade-off is cost: the machine is priced at a premium and you will keep buying bags and the occasional filter. A canister also needs a motorised head to do well on deep carpet, so check which floor tool comes with the exact version you buy. For a home that is mostly hard floor and low pile, it is hard to beat."
  },
  {
    "id": "hoover-windtunnel-3-max-performance-pet",
    "name": "Hoover WindTunnel 3 Max Performance Pet Upright",
    "category": "Bagless Upright, Pet Hair",
    "badge": "Best for Pet Hair on Carpet",
    "amazonUrl": "#",
    "pros": [
      "WindTunnel airflow design is built around lifting debris out of carpet",
      "Includes pet-focused tools aimed at upholstery and stairs",
      "Self-propelled drive on many versions reduces pushing effort on thick pile",
      "Corded convenience with no battery management",
      "Strong choice for wall-to-wall carpet in a multi-pet home"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "Large and heavy, so storage and carrying upstairs are real considerations",
      "Hose and attachments add clutter compared with a stick vacuum"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "If your home is mostly carpet and the fur never stops, this style of upright does the heavy lifting a stick vacuum cannot sustain.",
    "description": "Hoover has built its reputation on carpet, and the WindTunnel 3 Max Performance Pet is the corded upright we would look at first for a multi-pet home with wall-to-wall pile. The design routes airflow across the floor head to lift hair and dander from the carpet fibres, and the pet version adds tools intended for furniture and stairs. Check the current listing for the exact attachment bundle and filter details, because Hoover sells several WindTunnel variants and they differ in small ways. Owners commonly describe it as reliable on deep-pile carpet and good at keeping up with shedding dogs and cats. The weak spots are the same ones every full-size upright shares: it is bulky, it is heavy to carry upstairs, and the hose and tools take up room in a closet. If your floors are mostly hardwood or tile, a canister or a quality cordless stick will suit you better, but on carpet this is the workhorse."
  },
  {
    "id": "dyson-ball-animal-3",
    "name": "Dyson Ball Animal 3 Upright",
    "category": "Bagless Upright, Premium",
    "badge": "Best for Maneuverability",
    "amazonUrl": "#",
    "pros": [
      "Ball chassis pivots so the machine turns smoothly around furniture",
      "Floor head adjusts itself between carpet and hard floor",
      "Whole-machine filtration is a feature Dyson highlights for allergy households",
      "Bagless bin empties without touching the dirt on many versions",
      "Strong brand support and widely available spare parts"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "More expensive than comparable corded uprights from Shark or Hoover",
      "Still heavy, with the weight sitting high in the body"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "Worth the premium if you value steering and a refined, low-maintenance corded upright; otherwise the Shark does most of the job for less.",
    "description": "Dyson put the motor inside a ball, and the result is an upright that steers around chairs and table legs far more easily than a conventional design. The Ball Animal 3 is the corded model aimed at homes with pets, using a floor head that adjusts itself between carpet and hard floor so you do not have to flip a switch as you move between rooms. Dyson highlights whole-machine filtration, meaning the machine is designed so that air passes through filters rather than leaking past seals, which is the feature allergy buyers should look for in any vacuum. As with all Dyson uprights, the bagless bin is designed to empty cleanly with a single motion. You pay for the engineering: this sits at the premium end of corded uprights and is not noticeably lighter than the cheaper alternatives. Pick it if you hate steering a clumsy machine and want a brand with a strong parts network; skip it if budget is the main constraint."
  },
  {
    "id": "bissell-crosswave-pet-pro",
    "name": "Bissell CrossWave Pet Pro Wet-Dry Vacuum",
    "category": "Wet-Dry Multi-Surface (Hard Floors &amp; Area Rugs)",
    "badge": "Best for Mess &amp; Hard Floors",
    "amazonUrl": "#",
    "pros": [
      "Vacuums and washes in one pass, which cuts a two-step hard-floor routine to one",
      "Separate clean and dirty water tanks, so you are not pushing dirty water back onto the floor",
      "Handles sealed hardwood, tile, laminate and area rugs according to Bissell",
      "Useful for pet accidents and muddy paws",
      "Self-clean cycle for the brush roll and hoses reduces smell"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "Not a replacement for a full vacuum on wall-to-wall carpet",
      "Needs cleaning after use, or the tanks and brush roll develop odour"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "The add-on that fixes sticky, muddy, pet-stained hard floors. Treat it as a second machine, not your only vacuum.",
    "description": "The CrossWave is a different kind of machine, and including it makes sense because a lot of vacuum frustration comes from sticky or wet messes that a dry vacuum smears around. It vacuums and washes at the same time, with a clean-water tank feeding the brush roll and a separate dirty-water tank collecting the result. Bissell specifies it for sealed hard floors and area rugs, and the Pet Pro version adds a formula and filter aimed at pet households. For a kitchen with sticky spills or a hallway where dogs track in mud, it replaces the broom, the mop and the sweeping step with one pass. Just do not expect it to replace a standard vacuum: it is not intended for wall-to-wall carpet, and dry debris such as large crumbs is handled less cleanly than by a dedicated vacuum. You also have to clean the brush roll and tanks after each use. Used that way, as a partner to a main vacuum, it is excellent. For deeper carpet work, use a dedicated carpet cleaner instead."
  },
  {
    "id": "dyson-v8-cordless",
    "name": "Dyson V8 Cordless Stick Vacuum",
    "category": "Cordless Stick, Convenience",
    "badge": "Best Cordless Pick",
    "amazonUrl": "#",
    "pros": [
      "No cord, so a quick clean takes seconds from the charging dock",
      "Converts to a handheld for stairs, couches and the car",
      "Dyson rates the V8 for up to roughly 40 minutes in standard mode",
      "Light enough for stairs and above-floor cleaning",
      "Detachable battery on the V8 line means a failing battery can be swapped"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "Small bin that needs emptying often in a bigger home",
      "Runtime shortens sharply in max mode, and deep carpet will drain the battery"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "The right second vacuum, or the only one for a small apartment, where convenience beats raw capacity.",
    "description": "The Dyson V8 is here as the cordless representative, and as a deliberate trade-off. A stick vacuum wins the most important contest for daily cleaning: it is the one you will actually pull out, because it lives on a wall dock and has no cord to untangle. Dyson rates the V8 for up to roughly 40 minutes of runtime in its standard mode, but that figure falls quickly in the stronger setting, and on thick carpet a single charge covers far less. The bin is small, so a larger home means more frequent emptying. It converts to a handheld in seconds, which makes stairs, upholstery and cars easy. The battery on this line is user-replaceable, which is a point in its favour for long-term ownership. For most homes the V8 works best alongside a corded upright, not instead of one."
  },
  {
    "id": "irobot-roomba-694",
    "name": "iRobot Roomba 694 Robot Vacuum",
    "category": "Robot Vacuum, Budget",
    "badge": "Best Hands-Off Option",
    "amazonUrl": "#",
    "pros": [
      "Cleans on a schedule from the app, so floors stay baseline-clean without effort",
      "Wi-Fi connected, with voice assistant support",
      "Low profile slides under many sofas and beds",
      "Reasonable entry point into robot vacuuming from a well-known brand",
      "Dirt detection steers extra passes toward dirty patches"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "Navigates in a pattern rather than building a map, so coverage is less systematic than higher-end models",
      "Small bin and no self-emptying base, so you still empty it regularly"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "A good entry-level robot for maintaining floors between real vacuuming sessions. It is a helper, not a substitute for a full-power machine.",
    "description": "A robot vacuum is the most hands-off answer to the question of vacuum preference, and the Roomba 694 is the model we would suggest for a first robot. It runs on a schedule from the app, works with voice assistants and uses a low profile to slip under furniture. iRobot specifies a three-stage cleaning system and dirt detection that sends it back over heavily soiled areas. At this level it navigates in a pattern rather than building a floor map, which means it covers a room less methodically than a mapping robot, and it does not empty itself. If you want the robot to do the daily crumb and hair patrol while a proper vacuum handles the weekly deep clean, it is a sensible buy. For models with mapping, auto-emptying bases and stronger suction, look at a higher-tier robot."
  }
];

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      itemListElement: [
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          position: 1,
          name: "Home",
          item: "https://www.thehonestreviewers.com/",
        },
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          position: 2,
          name: "Best Lists",
          item: "https://www.thehonestreviewers.com/best-of/",
        },
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          position: 3,
          name: "Best Vacuum Cleaner",
          item: "https://www.thehonestreviewers.com/best-vacuum-cleaner/",
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      mainEntity: [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is the best type of vacuum cleaner for a home?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "It depends on your floors. Uprights suit carpet, canisters suit hard floors and stairs, sticks suit quick daily cleaning and robots suit hands-off upkeep. Many households do best with two machines: a corded vacuum for the weekly deep clean and a light cordless or robot for daily maintenance."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is a bagged or bagless vacuum better?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Bagged vacuums keep dust sealed until disposal, which is why they are usually suggested for allergies, but they cost more to run. Bagless models save on bags but need the bin emptied and filters cleaned. Choose according to which chore bothers you more, and whether you mind recurring costs."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do I need a HEPA vacuum?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "If you have allergies or asthma, a sealed system with proper HEPA filtration is worth having. If you do not, a standard filter is usually enough. Check that the vacuum is sealed, because a HEPA filter only works when air passes through it rather than leaking around the body."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is the best vacuum for pet hair?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "For carpet, a corded upright with a powered brush roll and good airflow, such as the Hoover or the Shark here, is hard to beat. For mixed floors, a Dyson with a self-adjusting head is a good all-rounder. Look for anti-wrap features, because long hair winding around the brush roll is the biggest annoyance."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How long should a vacuum cleaner last?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "It varies widely. Well-built canisters from premium brands are commonly reported to last a decade or more, while budget machines are often replaced in fewer years. Maintenance matters most: clean the brush roll, wash or replace filters and keep the hose clear, and a machine will last far longer."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Are cordless vacuums as powerful as corded ones?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Modern cordless vacuums are good for daily cleaning, but they generally do not match a corded upright on deep carpet, and runtime drops in their strongest mode. They are best treated as convenient companions to a corded machine unless your home is small and mostly hard floor."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can a robot vacuum replace my regular vacuum?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "For most homes, not entirely. A robot keeps floors tidy between deep cleans and is excellent for crumbs and pet hair on hard floors, but it will not clean stairs, upholstery or thick carpet as well as a full vacuum. Read our guide on whether robot vacuums are worth it for the full picture."
          }
        }
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: title,
      author: authorSchema(Astro.url.pathname),
      datePublished: dates.published,
      dateModified: dates.modified,
      publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "The Honest Reviewers" },
    },
    {
      "@type": "ItemList",
      name: title,
      numberOfItems: PRODUCTS.length,
      itemListElement: PRODUCTS.map((product, index) => ({
        "@type": "ListItem",
        position: index + 1,
        name: product.name,
        url: new URL(`#${product.id}`, Astro.url).toString(),
      })),
    },
    ...PRODUCTS.map((product) => ({
      "@type": "Product",
      name: product.name,
      description: product.description,
      brand: {
        "@type": "Brand",
        name: product.name.split(" ")[0],
      },
    })),
  ],
};
---

<Layout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  ogType="article"
  article={{
    publishedTime: dates.published,
    modifiedTime: dates.modified,
    author: authorName(Astro.url.pathname),
    section: "Home Appliances",
    tags: [
      "best vacuum cleaner",
      "vacuum cleaner",
      "best upright vacuum",
      "bagged vs bagless vacuum",
      "best vacuum for pet hair",
      "vacuum cleaner for allergies"
    ],
  }}
  jsonLd={schema}
>
  <article class="relative overflow-hidden">
    <!-- Hero Section -->
    <div class="bg-gray-900 py-16 lg:py-24 relative overflow-hidden">
      <div class="absolute inset-0 opacity-10" style="background-image: radial-gradient(circle at 20% 20%, #38BDF8 0, transparent 45%), radial-gradient(circle at 80% 60%, #FF4500 0, transparent 40%);"></div>
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 relative z-10 text-center">
        <div class="flex justify-center mb-6">
          <TrustBadge />
        </div>
        <div class="flex justify-center gap-3 mb-6">
          <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#FF4500]/20 text-[#FF4500] text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest border border-[#FF4500]/30">
            Buyer's Guide
          </span>
          <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-green-500/10 text-green-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest border border-green-500/20">
            Buyer's Guide
          </span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-4xl lg:text-6xl font-black text-white leading-tight mb-8">
          Best Vacuum <span class="text-[#38BDF8]">Cleaners</span> for Your Home
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-8 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
          The best vacuum depends on your floors, your pets and how much you hate emptying a bin. Here are seven worth buying, and who each one is for.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center">
          <a
            href="#shark-navigator-lift-away"
            class="px-8 py-4 bg-[#FF4500] hover:bg-[#E63E00] text-white font-black rounded-xl shadow-lg transition-all no-underline"
          >
            See Our #1 Pick
          </a>
          <a
            href="#top-picks"
            class="px-8 py-4 bg-white/10 hover:bg-white/20 text-white font-bold rounded-xl border border-white/10 no-underline"
          >
            Jump to the Top Picks
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Author & Meta -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pt-12">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-6 border-b border-gray-100 pb-8">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <AuthorAvatar size={48} />
          <div>
            <p class="text-sm font-bold text-gray-900">Shaheer Ali Khan</p>
            <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-widest">Consumer Product Testing &amp; Materials Performance Specialist</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="h-10 w-px bg-gray-200 hidden sm:block"></div>
        <div class="hidden sm:block">
          <p class="text-sm font-bold text-gray-900">Last Updated</p>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-500">{dates.display}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="hidden sm:block ml-auto">
          <SocialProof users="12.4k" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Table of Contents -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-10">
      <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 lg:p-8">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-black text-gray-900 mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
          In This Guide
        </h2>
        <nav class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-2">
          <a href="#choose-by-preference" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">1. Start With What You Prefer</a>
          <a href="#top-picks" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">2. Our 7 Top Picks Reviewed</a>
          <a href="#vacuum-types" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">3. Upright, Canister, Stick or Robot</a>
          <a href="#bagged-vs-bagless" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">4. Bagged vs Bagless</a>
          <a href="#filtration-allergies" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">5. Filtration and Allergies</a>
          <a href="#pets-and-floors" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">6. Pet Hair, Carpet and Hard Floors</a>
          <a href="#budget-ownership" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">7. Budget and True Cost</a>
          <a href="#care-and-storage" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">8. Maintenance and Storage</a>
          <a href="#mistakes" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">9. Common Mistakes</a>
          <a href="#faq" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">10. FAQ</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Content -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pb-16 lg:pb-24">
      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p class="text-2xl font-medium text-gray-900 mb-8 italic">
          There is no single best vacuum cleaner, only the best one for the way you clean. A corded upright wins on thick carpet, a bagged canister wins for allergies, a stick wins on convenience and a robot wins when you would rather not do it at all. We matched seven widely sold models to those preferences, using manufacturer specifications and what owners commonly report, so you can pick the one that fits your home.
        </p>

        <QuickPicks products={PRODUCTS} />

        <div id="choose-by-preference" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            1. Start With What You Prefer, Not With the Spec Sheet
          </h2>

          <p>
            Most vacuum buying guides start with suction numbers, but suction is the wrong place to begin. Wattage and airflow figures are not measured the same way across brands, so a bigger number on the box rarely tells you which machine will clean your floors better. A more useful starting point is the set of preferences that decide whether you will actually enjoy using the thing: how heavy you are willing to carry, whether you accept a cord, whether you will touch a dusty bag, and what your floors are made of.
          </p>

          <p>
            Those preferences sort buyers quickly. If you dislike cords and clean in short bursts, a cordless stick wins. If you hate emptying dirt, a bagged machine or a robot suits you. If you have wall-to-wall carpet and a shedding dog, an upright with a powered brush is the sensible choice. If your home is hardwood and tile, a canister or a wet-dry machine handles it better. Write your answers down before you read the picks below, because the right machine falls out of them.
          </p>

          <p>
            The honest truth is that no single vacuum is best for every home. The cheapest effective setup for many households is two machines: a full-size corded vacuum for the weekly deep clean and a light cordless or robot for the daily pickup. That is why this list mixes categories instead of ranking seven uprights against each other. We have kept our attention on models that exist and are widely sold, and described them using manufacturer specifications and what owners commonly report rather than inventing lab numbers.
          </p>

          <p>
            As with the rest of our buying guides, a few of the links below are affiliate links, and we earn a commission if you buy through them at no extra cost to you. That has not changed what we recommend: the Shark sits at number one because it is the best value, not because of what it pays. If a pick is not right for your preferences, we say so in the cons and the bottom line.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Picks -->
        <div id="top-picks" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            2. The 7 Best Vacuum Cleaners, Ranked by Who They Suit
          </h2>

          <p>
            Each pick below is described using the manufacturer's published specifications and what owners commonly report, not invented lab results. Links on this page are affiliate links: if you buy through them we earn a commission at no extra cost to you, and it does not change the order of the list. Always check the current listing and model number before you buy, since brands sell close variants.
          </p>

          {PRODUCTS.map((product, index) => (
            <div id={product.id} class="scroll-mt-24 mt-12 first:mt-8">
