            The best vacuum cleaner is the one that matches your floors and your habits. Buy the Shark Navigator if you want one dependable, affordable machine; the Miele if allergies or longevity come first; the Hoover if carpet and pets rule your house; and the Dyson Ball if steering and refinement are worth a premium.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Add the Dyson V8 or the Roomba 694 when daily convenience matters, and the Bissell CrossWave when hard-floor messes are the problem. Check the current listing and model number before you buy, and remember that a vacuum you maintain will outlast one you do not.
